A sticker for this device.

The undo sticker is slot's about box: a device compliance plate, with the
credits as its compliance block and an "ANBERNIC RG SP" wordmark. On the Miyoo
it was describing hardware that is not there -- model AGS-102, BaseOS by
pvaibhav -- and naming the wrong handheld in the largest type on the screen.

So: the model row names the Mini Flip, the OS line names Miyoo's own
firmware, and the credits say in so many words that the frontend is slot, by
Brandon Kowalski, written for the Anbernic RG SP, and that this is an
unofficial port -- which the sticker is the right place to say, because it is
the only screen a user reads for provenance. Upstream's copyright line stays as
it is and a port line goes under it.

The wordmark is regenerated by `tools/wordmark.py` from `assets/label.ttf`:
Open Sans Bold, which the sticker already ships and already credits, with the
first word obliqued the way upstream slants "ANBERNIC". Same two-layer
structure as upstream's -- dark fill over a white stroke, glyphs already
outlined -- so the renderer still needs no font.

The origin row sets its own type size: two cities do not fit beside the barcode
panel at the body size.

This changes what the frontend says about itself rather than how it behaves.
It is a UX change, deliberately, and it is scoped to the sticker.

Applies to upstream 91499a9.

